# One worker per line: "username,webhook_url"
#
# When a creator posts a new task, the app computes eligibility immediately
# (required_skills is mandatory) and pings ONLY the workers who currently
# qualify - looked up here by username. Anyone not eligible for a given
# task, or not listed here at all, hears nothing about it. This is
# different from teams_webhooks_creators.txt, which broadcasts to a flat
# list rather than filtering per person.
#
# The username must match a worker's login username exactly (see the
# Workers page or seed.py). The webhook URL is a personal Incoming Webhook
# for that worker - e.g. a 1:1 chat or personal channel they've configured:
#   1. In Microsoft Teams, open the chat/channel where that worker wants
#      their task pings.
#   2. Channel menu (...) -> Connectors -> Incoming Webhook -> Configure.
#   3. Give it a name and copy the generated URL.
#   4. Add a line below: worker_username,https://...
#
# Maintained directly by admins by editing this file on the server - not
# exposed through the web UI. Copy this file to teams_webhooks_workers.txt
# (drop the .example) and fill in real usernames/URLs; that file is
# gitignored since each URL can post on its own (treat it like a secret).
#
# Blank lines, lines starting with #, and lines without a comma are ignored.
#
# worker1,https://outlook.office.com/webhook/...
# worker2,https://outlook.office.com/webhook/...
